# Mood-Abaya Project Architecture & Conventions

## Tech Stack

- **Framework:** Laravel 11+ with nwidart/laravel-modules
- **Frontend:** Blade templates, Tailwind CSS, Vanilla JS
- **Language:** PHP 8.2+, bilingual (English + Arabic), RTL support
- **Database:** MySQL, Eloquent ORM with translatable JSON columns
- **Build:** Vite (`vite.config.js`, `vite-module-loader.js`)

---

## Module Architecture

Each domain has its own module. Modules contain **both** frontend and admin code. Admin code lives in `Admin/` subdirectories. Each module owns its views under `resources/views/admin/` and `resources/views/frontend/`.

```
Modules/{Module}/
├── app/Http/Controllers/
│   ├── Admin/              ← Admin controllers (back-office)
│   │   └── XxxController.php
│   └── XxxController.php   ← Frontend controllers (customer-facing)
├── app/Http/Requests/
│   ├── Admin/              ← Admin form requests
│   │   └── XxxRequest.php
│   └── XxxRequest.php      ← Frontend form requests
├── app/Services/
│   ├── Admin/              ← Admin services
│   │   └── XxxService.php
│   └── XxxService.php      ← Frontend services
├── app/Providers/
│   ├── {Module}ServiceProvider.php  ← Registers views, blade components
│   └── RouteServiceProvider.php     ← Loads web.php AND admin.php
├── routes/
│   ├── web.php             ← Frontend routes
│   ├── admin.php           ← Admin routes (prefix: admin, middleware: auth+is_admin)
│   └── api.php             ← API routes (if any)
├── resources/views/
│   ├── admin/              ← Admin blade views for this module
│   └── frontend/           ← Frontend blade views for this module
└── module.json
```

### 13 Modules

| Module | Admin (back-office) | Frontend (customer-facing) |
|--------|--------------------|-----------------------------|
| **Core** | Dashboard | Home page, About, Maintenance |
| **Settings** | Site settings, Frontend settings, Translations | *(none)* |
| **User** | User management | *(none)* |
| **Shop** | Products, Categories, Reviews | Product listing, category pages, search |
| **Order** | Order management, export, shipping | Checkout, order confirmation |
| **Payment** | Payment management, approval | Payment processing |
| **Contact** | Contact messages | Contact form |
| **Cart** | *(none)* | Cart management |
| **Testimonial** | Testimonial management | *(none)* |
| **Newsletter** | Newsletter subscribers | Newsletter subscribe (POST) |
| **Blog** | Blog post management | Blog listing, single post |
| **Page** | Static page content editing | About page, dynamic pages |
| **Faq** | FAQ management | *(displayed on contact page)* |

### Admin Route Registration

Each module's `RouteServiceProvider` loads admin routes:

```php
protected function mapAdminRoutes(): void
{
    Route::middleware(['web', 'auth', 'verified', 'is_admin'])
        ->prefix('admin')
        ->name('admin.')
        ->group(module_path($this->name, '/routes/admin.php'));
}
```

All admin route names start with `admin.` (e.g., `admin.products.index`, `admin.orders.show`).

