## When Adding a New Feature

1. Identify the **module** (or create a new one if it's a new domain)
2. Create the **Model** in `app/Models/`
3. Create the **Migration** in `database/migrations/`
4. Create the **Service** in `Modules/{Mod}/app/Services/` (frontend) or `Admin/` (admin)
5. Create **FormRequest** class(es) in `Modules/{Mod}/app/Http/Requests/` or `Admin/`
6. Create the **Controller** (thin) in `Modules/{Mod}/app/Http/Controllers/` or `Admin/`
7. Add **routes** in `routes/web.php` (frontend) or `routes/admin.php` (admin)
8. Create **Blade views** in `Modules/{Mod}/resources/views/admin/` or `frontend/`
9. Reference views as `mod::admin.xxx` or `mod::frontend.xxx`
10. Add **CSS** to `public/css/admin/` or `public/css/frontend/`
11. Add **JS** to `public/js/admin/` or `public/js/frontend/`
12. Add **translations** to `lang/en.json` and `lang/ar.json`

### Creating a New Module

```bash
php artisan module:make {ModuleName}
```

Then ensure the module's `ServiceProvider` has `registerViews()` and its `RouteServiceProvider` has `mapAdminRoutes()`:

```php
// ServiceProvider — register views
public function registerViews(): void
{
    $sourcePath = module_path($this->name, 'resources/views');
    $this->loadViewsFrom([$sourcePath], $this->nameLower);
}

// RouteServiceProvider — load admin routes
protected function mapAdminRoutes(): void
{
    Route::middleware(['web', 'auth', 'verified', 'is_admin'])
        ->prefix('admin')
        ->name('admin.')
        ->group(module_path($this->name, '/routes/admin.php'));
}
```

### Namespace Convention

```
Modules\{Module}\Http\Controllers\Admin\{Name}Controller   ← Admin controller
Modules\{Module}\Http\Controllers\{Name}Controller          ← Frontend controller
Modules\{Module}\Services\Admin\{Name}Service               ← Admin service
Modules\{Module}\Services\{Name}Service                     ← Frontend service
Modules\{Module}\Http\Requests\Admin\{Name}Request          ← Admin form request
Modules\{Module}\Http\Requests\{Name}Request                ← Frontend form request
```
